.TH BLUETEAM 8 "December 2024" "BlueTeam 2.0.0" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
blueteam \- BlueTeam Linux Enterprise Security Monitoring Platform
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B blueteam
[\fICOMMAND\fR] [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B BlueTeam
is an enterprise-grade security monitoring and threat detection platform for Linux systems.
It provides real-time system monitoring, machine learning-based threat detection, and
automated incident response capabilities.
.PP
The platform consists of 23 integrated security modules across 6 security domains:
.IP \(bu 2
Network Defense (5 modules)
.IP \(bu 2
Endpoint Security (5 modules)
.IP \(bu 2
Vulnerability Management (4 modules)
.IP \(bu 2
Identity & Access Control (3 modules)
.IP \(bu 2
Incident Response (3 modules)
.IP \(bu 2
Advanced AI Threat Detection (3 modules)
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
Show the current status of the BlueTeam daemon and recent threats.
.TP
.B start
Start the BlueTeam security daemon.
.TP
.B stop
Stop the BlueTeam security daemon.
.TP
.B logs
[\fB-n\fR \fINUMBER\fR]
Show daemon logs. Use \fB-n\fR to specify number of lines (default: 50).
.TP
.B threats
[\fB-l\fR \fILIMIT\fR]
Display detected threats. Use \fB-l\fR to limit number of threats displayed.
.TP
.B config
[\fBshow\fR|\fBedit\fR]
Manage BlueTeam configuration. Use \fBshow\fR to display current config or \fBedit\fR
to modify it with an editor.
.TP
.B version
Display BlueTeam version information.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show help message and exit.
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-version
Show version information and exit.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The main configuration file is located at:
.IP
/etc/blueteam/blueteam.conf
.PP
Key configuration sections:
.TP
.B [daemon]
General daemon settings including monitoring interval and log level.
.TP
.B [network]
Network monitoring configuration including suspicious ports.
.TP
.B [processes]
Process monitoring settings and suspicious process patterns.
.TP
.B [files]
File integrity monitoring for critical system files.
.TP
.B [ml]
Machine learning threat detection settings.
.TP
.B [alerting]
Alert destination configuration (syslog, email, Slack, PagerDuty).
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /etc/blueteam/blueteam.conf
Main configuration file.
.TP
.B /var/lib/blueteam/
Data storage directory for threats and metrics.
.TP
.B /var/log/blueteam/daemon.log
Daemon log file.
.TP
.B /var/run/blueteam.pid
Daemon process ID file.
.TP
.B /etc/systemd/system/blueteam.service
Systemd service file.
.SH SYSTEMD INTEGRATION
BlueTeam is integrated with systemd for automatic startup and management:
.TP
.B Enable at boot:
.IP
systemctl enable blueteam
.TP
.B Start service:
.IP
systemctl start blueteam
.TP
.B Stop service:
.IP
systemctl stop blueteam
.TP
.B View service status:
.IP
systemctl status blueteam
.TP
.B View service logs:
.IP
journalctl -u blueteam -f
.SH SECURITY MODULES
.TP
.B Network Defense
AI Traffic Analyzer, Zero-Trust Firewall, Intrusion Detection System,
VPN & Secure Tunneling, DNS Security Filter
.TP
.B Endpoint Security
Malware Scanner, Process Sentinel, Kernel Hardening,
Registry/Config Guard, USB/Hardware Blocker
.TP
.B Vulnerability Management
Auto-Patch Manager, Compliance Auditor, Vulnerability Scanner,
Secret Scanner
.TP
.B Identity & Access
Biometric/MFA Gateway, Privilege Escalation Monitor,
Session Hijacking Guard
.TP
.B Incident Response
Log Aggregator (SIEM), Snapshot & Recovery, Live Forensics Toolkit
.TP
.B Advanced AI
Threat Intelligence Feed, Automated Playbook Engine,
AI Security Assistant, Decoy/Honeypot Deployer
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Check daemon status:
.IP
blueteam status
.TP
View recent threats:
.IP
blueteam threats -l 20
.TP
View last 100 log lines:
.IP
blueteam logs -n 100
.TP
Edit configuration:
.IP
blueteam config edit
.TP
Start daemon:
.IP
sudo systemctl start blueteam
.SH PERFORMANCE
.TP
.B Memory Usage:
150-200MB (all 23 modules running)
.TP
.B CPU Usage:
<5% idle, <20% under load
.TP
.B Threat Detection Latency:
<100ms
.TP
.B Database Size:
~50MB after 1 week of operation
.SH REQUIREMENTS
.IP \(bu 2
Python 3.8 or later
.IP \(bu 2
Linux kernel 4.4 or later
.IP \(bu 2
Root/sudo access for system monitoring
.IP \(bu 2
150MB+ available disk space
